# Sphinx Documentation Best Practices

## Overview

Sphinx is a powerful documentation generator that transforms reStructuredText and Markdown sources into beautiful, searchable documentation. Originally created for Python documentation, it now supports multiple programming languages and documentation styles.

## Core Principles

- Use Sphinx for generating comprehensive technical documentation from reStructuredText sources
- Structure documentation with proper toctree organization and hierarchical content layout
- Use appropriate Sphinx directives and roles for rich documentation formatting
- Implement cross-references and intersphinx linking for connected documentation ecosystems
- Configure Sphinx themes and extensions for enhanced documentation presentation
- Use autodoc extensions for automatic API documentation generation from code
- Implement proper code highlighting and example integration with sphinx-gallery or similar
- Configure multiple output formats (HTML, PDF, EPUB) for diverse documentation needs
- Use internationalization features for multi-language documentation support
- Integrate with version control and CI/CD for automated documentation deployment

## Project Setup

### Installation and Initialization

```bash
# Install Sphinx
pip install sphinx sphinx-rtd-theme sphinx-autodoc-typehints

# Quick start
sphinx-quickstart docs

# Build documentation
cd docs
make html
```

### Configuration (conf.py)

```python
# docs/source/conf.py
import os
import sys
from datetime import datetime

# Add project root to Python path for autodoc
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.abspath('../..'))

# Project information
project = 'My Project'
copyright = f'{datetime.now().year}, Your Name'
author = 'Your Name'
release = '1.0.0'

# General configuration
extensions = [
    'sphinx.ext.autodoc',
    'sphinx.ext.napoleon',
    'sphinx.ext.viewcode',
    'sphinx.ext.intersphinx',
    'sphinx.ext.coverage',
    'sphinx.ext.todo',
    'sphinx.ext.autosummary',
    'sphinx_rtd_theme',
    'sphinx_autodoc_typehints',
    'sphinx_copybutton',
    'myst_parser',  # For Markdown support
]

# Extension settings
autodoc_default_options = {
    'members': True,
    'member-order': 'bysource',
    'special-members': '__init__',
    'undoc-members': True,
    'exclude-members': '__weakref__'
}

# Napoleon settings for Google/NumPy style docstrings
napoleon_google_docstring = True
napoleon_numpy_docstring = True
napoleon_include_init_with_doc = True
napoleon_include_private_with_doc = False
napoleon_include_special_with_doc = True
napoleon_use_admonition_for_examples = True
napoleon_use_admonition_for_notes = True
napoleon_use_admonition_for_references = False
napoleon_use_ivar = False
napoleon_use_param = True
napoleon_use_rtype = True

# Intersphinx mapping
intersphinx_mapping = {
    'python': ('https://docs.python.org/3', None),
    'numpy': ('https://numpy.org/doc/stable/', None),
    'pandas': ('https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/', None),
}

# Theme configuration
html_theme = 'sphinx_rtd_theme'
html_theme_options = {
    'navigation_depth': 4,
    'collapse_navigation': False,
    'sticky_navigation': True,
    'includehidden': True,
    'titles_only': False,
    'display_version': True,
    'prev_next_buttons_location': 'bottom',
}

# Static files
html_static_path = ['_static']
html_css_files = ['custom.css']
html_js_files = ['custom.js']

# Logo and favicon
html_logo = '_static/logo.png'
html_favicon = '_static/favicon.ico'

# Source suffix
source_suffix = {
    '.rst': 'restructuredtext',
    '.md': 'markdown',
}

# Master doc
master_doc = 'index'

# Exclude patterns
exclude_patterns = ['_build', 'Thumbs.db', '.DS_Store', '**.ipynb_checkpoints']

# Pygments style
pygments_style = 'sphinx'

# -- Options for HTML output
html_show_sourcelink = True
html_sidebars = {
    '**': [
        'globaltoc.html',
        'relations.html',
        'sourcelink.html',
        'searchbox.html',
    ]
}

# -- Options for PDF output
latex_elements = {
    'papersize': 'letterpaper',
    'pointsize': '10pt',
    'preamble': r'''
\usepackage{charter}
\usepackage[defaultsans]{lato}
\usepackage{inconsolata}
    ''',
}

# Grouping the document tree
latex_documents = [
    (master_doc, 'project.tex', 'Project Documentation',
     'Your Name', 'manual'),
]
```

