## Best Practices

### Do's
- Write comprehensive docstrings in your code
- Use semantic markup for better structure
- Include code examples and tutorials
- Keep documentation close to code
- Use version control for documentation
- Test documentation builds in CI/CD
- Include API examples with expected output
- Use cross-references liberally

### Don'ts
- Don't use hard-coded paths
- Don't ignore build warnings
- Don't mix tabs and spaces in RST
- Don't use excessive nesting in toctrees
- Don't forget to update documentation
- Don't use screenshots for code
- Don't skip proofreading

This comprehensive guide ensures professional technical documentation with Sphinx.

- Configure multiple output formats (HTML, PDF, EPUB) for diverse documentation needs.
- Use internationalization features for multi-language documentation support.
- Integrate with version control and CI/CD for automated documentation deployment.
